SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"IMF Executive Board Concludes 2022 Article IV Consultation and the Second Review Under the Extended Credit Facility Arrangement for the Democratic Republic of the Congo","publisher":"IMF","publication_date":"2022-06-29","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/news/articles/2022/06/29/pr22240-democratic-republic-of-congo","claim":"The IMF said the authorities had adopted prudent macroeconomic policies, most visibly by halting central bank financing to the government.","locator":"line 242","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary IMF press release with explicit policy attribution and date.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target-period macro policy evidence.","ruler_attribution":"High: this describes the national authorities under Tshisekedi's government.","contrary_evidence":["The same release says poverty remained very high and domestic arrears accumulated."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"IMF Executive Board Concludes 2022 Article IV Consultation and the Second Review Under the Extended Credit Facility Arrangement for the Democratic Republic of the Congo","publisher":"IMF","publication_date":"2022-06-29","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/news/articles/2022/06/29/pr22240-democratic-republic-of-congo","claim":"The IMF said fragility continued to hinder inclusive growth, with 72.5 percent of the population in poverty and basic public services severely under-provisioned.","locator":"line 244","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary IMF press release with direct macro and household welfare assessment.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target-period welfare context.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate: these are national outcomes under the incumbent government, but not all are uniquely ruler-caused.","contrary_evidence":["The same release reports growth at 6.2 percent in 2021 and stronger reserves."],"lenses":["5B.8","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"IMF Executive Board Concludes 2022 Article IV Consultation and the Second Review Under the Extended Credit Facility Arrangement for the Democratic Republic of the Congo","publisher":"IMF","publication_date":"2022-06-29","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/news/articles/2022/06/29/pr22240-democratic-republic-of-congo","claim":"The IMF said the program remained satisfactory but that one structural benchmark was pending because a mining contract had not yet been published and two end-June 2022 benchmarks were slightly delayed.","locator":"line 245","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary IMF program-monitoring report with clear implementation detail.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target-period implementation evidence.","ruler_attribution":"High: this is about government implementation under Tshisekedi's administration.","contrary_evidence":["The same report says four of five structural benchmarks were met."],"lenses":["5B.4","5B.5","5B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"IMF Executive Board Concludes 2022 Article IV Consultation and the Second Review Under the Extended Credit Facility Arrangement for the Democratic Republic of the Congo","publisher":"IMF","publication_date":"2022-06-29","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/news/articles/2022/06/29/pr22240-democratic-republic-of-congo","claim":"The IMF urged continued efforts to improve mining sector transparency, the anti-corruption and AML/CFT frameworks, the business climate, and governance to support diversification and competitiveness.","locator":"lines 257-257 and 266-266","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary IMF guidance tied to the country's reform program.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target-period reform guidance.","ruler_attribution":"High: the policy recommendations are directed at the incumbent authorities.","contrary_evidence":["The same release says external shocks and inflation were still weighing on households."],"lenses":["5B.4","5B.5","5B.6","5B.7","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"IMF Staff Completes 2022 Article IV and Program Review Mission to the Democratic Republic of the Congo","publisher":"IMF","publication_date":"2022-05-09","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/news/articles/2022/05/09/pr22144-imf-staff-completes-2022-article-iv-program-review-mission-to-democratic-republic-of-congo","claim":"IMF staff said sustaining reform efforts to improve public finance management, the business climate and governance remained critical to promote inclusive growth.","locator":"line 247","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary IMF mission statement from 2022 with direct reform assessment.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target-period policy assessment.","ruler_attribution":"High: the mission assessed the incumbent government's policy agenda.","contrary_evidence":["The same statement says the economy still faced spillovers from the war in Ukraine."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.3","5B.6","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"IMF Staff Completes 2022 Article IV and Program Review Mission to the Democratic Republic of the Congo","publisher":"IMF","publication_date":"2022-05-09","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/news/articles/2022/05/09/pr22144-imf-staff-completes-2022-article-iv-program-review-mission-to-democratic-republic-of-congo","claim":"The mission said the authorities should reform fuel subsidies, contain current spending, and create space for targeted social transfers, while improving public investment and fiscal governance.","locator":"lines 258-261","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary IMF mission statement with specific fiscal and distributional policy advice.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target-period policy implementation agenda.","ruler_attribution":"High: this concerns government policy choices under Tshisekedi.","contrary_evidence":["The same statement notes significant downside risks and inflation pressures."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.6","5B.8","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Democratic Republic of Congo Economic Update: Harnessing Growth Through Digital Connectivity to Create Jobs and Reduce Poverty","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-10-07","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/10/07/democratic-republic-of-congo-economic-update","claim":"The World Bank said poverty reduction had been elusive and the benefits from growth were not yet being shared more widely.","locator":"lines 139-142","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary World Bank country update with explicit welfare interpretation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target-period welfare assessment.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate: strong context and outcome evidence, but not all distributional outcomes are uniquely ruler-attributable.","contrary_evidence":["The same update says economic resilience was strong and growth had rebounded."],"lenses":["5B.8","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Democratic Republic of Congo Economic Update: Harnessing Growth Through Digital Connectivity to Create Jobs and Reduce Poverty","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-10-07","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/10/07/democratic-republic-of-congo-economic-update","claim":"The World Bank said a 10 percent higher broadband penetration rate could add about 2.5 percent of GDP and generate close to 700,000 jobs, and it praised the government's liberalization of the telecommunications sector.","locator":"lines 143-147","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary World Bank analysis with a quantified policy pathway.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 policy path and medium-term reform evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate: this supports a pro-investment policy direction under the incumbent government.","contrary_evidence":["The same update says the digital divide remained stark and geographic and socio-economic disparities persisted."],"lenses":["5B.4","5B.6","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Budget 2022","publisher":"Ministère du Budget, DRC","publication_date":"2022-03-31","url":"https://budget.gouv.cd/budget-2022/","claim":"The Ministry of Budget's 2022 budget page shows the law on finances for 2022, Law No. 21/029 of 31 December 2021, and the linked budget documents for 2022.","locator":"lines 70-81","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct official budget portal with the named 2022 finance law.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 fiscal framework evidence.","ruler_attribution":"High: this is the incumbent government's approved fiscal framework.","contrary_evidence":["Budget approval alone does not establish implementation quality."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.6","5B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Projet de Loi de Finances pour l'exercice 2022","publisher":"Ministère du Budget, DRC","publication_date":"2021-09-01","url":"https://budget.gouv.cd/wp-content/uploads/budget2022/projet/document_1_expose_des_motifs_et_annexes_loi_plf_2022_vs_final.pdf","claim":"The 2022 budget proposal says the government intended to continue basic education free of charge, universal health coverage, population census and election preparation, tax reform, and protection of purchasing power.","locator":"lines 24-34","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official budget proposal with explicit policy priorities.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Pre-2022 planning for the target year.","ruler_attribution":"High: these are declared government priorities under Tshisekedi's administration.","contrary_evidence":["These are announced priorities, not proof of delivery."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.6","5B.8","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Projet de Loi de Finances pour l'exercice 2022","publisher":"Ministère du Budget, DRC","publication_date":"2021-09-01","url":"https://budget.gouv.cd/wp-content/uploads/budget2022/projet/document_1_expose_des_motifs_et_annexes_loi_plf_2022_vs_final.pdf","claim":"The 2022 budget proposal said the government would intensify the fight against corruption and revenue leakage, relying on expected improvements in commodity prices and better monetary and budget coordination.","locator":"lines 35-43","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official budget text with explicit anti-corruption and revenue claims.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Pre-2022 target-period planning.","ruler_attribution":"High: explicit government intent under the incumbent administration.","contrary_evidence":["The budget text states the plan, not the realized outcome."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.5","5B.7","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Projet de Loi de Finances pour l'exercice 2022","publisher":"Ministère du Budget, DRC","publication_date":"2021-09-01","url":"https://budget.gouv.cd/wp-content/uploads/budget2022/projet/document_1_expose_des_motifs_et_annexes_loi_plf_2022_vs_final.pdf","claim":"The 2022 budget proposal assumed 5.6 percent GDP growth, 6.2 percent average inflation, and a 41.8 percent increase in the central government budget relative to 2021.","locator":"lines 44-56","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official macro assumptions and fiscal envelope in the budget bill.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Pre-2022 fiscal planning and macro assumptions.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate: this reflects planned fiscal policy more than realized performance.","contrary_evidence":["Assumptions are not outcomes; later IMF data show inflation and shocks were worse than planned."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Projet de Loi de Finances pour l'exercice 2022","publisher":"Ministère du Budget, DRC","publication_date":"2021-09-01","url":"https://budget.gouv.cd/wp-content/uploads/budget2022/projet/document_2_expose_general_plf_2022_et_annexes_vs_finale.pdf","claim":"The budget framework said revenue policy would raise domestic resources through anti-fraud and tax reforms, and it prioritized social and productive investment, east-region peace, and the 2023 general elections.","locator":"lines 121-126","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official budget framework with explicit policy priorities.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Pre-2022 target-period policy planning.","ruler_attribution":"High: this is declared executive budget policy.","contrary_evidence":["Announced priorities do not show execution quality."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.4","5B.6","5B.8","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"World Bank Supports the Democratic Republic of Congo’s Efforts to Improve Public Resources Management and Service Delivery","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2021-12-16","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2021/12/16/world-bank-supports-the-democratic-republic-of-congo-s-efforts-to-improve-public-resources-management-and-service-delive","claim":"The World Bank approved a project to increase mining revenue transparency and strengthen expenditure management at the central level and in selected provinces so that more funds reach public service delivery.","locator":"lines 148-150","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary World Bank project announcement with direct fiscal-governance objective.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Pre-2022 reform baseline for the target year.","ruler_attribution":"High: this is a government-supported reform package in the Tshisekedi period.","contrary_evidence":["The project was approved because the underlying revenue and expenditure systems still needed strengthening."],"lenses":["5B.4","5B.5","5B.6","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"World Bank Supports the Democratic Republic of Congo’s Efforts to Improve Public Resources Management and Service Delivery","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2021-12-16","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2021/12/16/world-bank-supports-the-democratic-republic-of-congo-s-efforts-to-improve-public-resources-management-and-service-delive","claim":"The project would support a single treasury account, better budget control, improved annual reporting, stronger oversight by the Court of Accounts, and enhanced civil-society participation in budgeting.","locator":"lines 150-152","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary project design statement with concrete institutional reforms.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Pre-2022 reform implementation context.","ruler_attribution":"High: the reforms are tied to the incumbent government's public financial management agenda.","contrary_evidence":["The statement itself implies the reforms were still needed, so this is not evidence of success by itself."],"lenses":["5B.4","5B.5","5B.6","5B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"The Democratic Republic of the Congo has achieved a high overall score in implementing the 2019 EITI Standard","publisher":"EITI","publication_date":"2022-10-13","url":"https://eiti.org/board-decision/2022-50","claim":"The EITI Board commended the DRC for the timeliness of its disclosures and its thematic reports on SOEs, licensing, contract disclosure, beneficial ownership, subnational transfers, mining royalties, and barter-type infrastructure provisions.","locator":"line 92","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent international validation of disclosure practices.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 institutional transparency evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate: strong institutional transparency evidence, but not a direct measure of household welfare.","contrary_evidence":["The same decision says beneficial ownership and some newer standards were not yet fully implemented."],"lenses":["5B.4","5B.5","5B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"The Democratic Republic of the Congo has achieved a high overall score in implementing the 2019 EITI Standard","publisher":"EITI","publication_date":"2022-10-13","url":"https://eiti.org/board-decision/2022-50","claim":"The EITI Secretariat said the DRC had only partly met the beneficial-ownership objective and that only 21 of 77 significant extractive licensees submitted beneficial-ownership information in the cited report period.","locator":"lines 449-453","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent validation report with a concrete quantitative gap.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Relevant 2022 transparency and anti-capture context.","ruler_attribution":"High: this is about extractive-sector transparency under the incumbent government.","contrary_evidence":["The same report notes some progress in open-format disclosure."],"lenses":["5B.4","5B.5","5B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Financial crime watchdog adds Congo to money laundering watch list","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-10-09","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/10/09/congo-corruption","claim":"Reuters reported that the Financial Action Task Force planned to place the DRC on its grey list for shortcomings in stamping out financial corruption, including money laundering and anti-terrorist financing.","locator":"lines 610-613","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters-sourced report with clear attribution to FATF and finance ministry statements.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 governance and financial-integrity evidence.","ruler_attribution":"High: this is about national anti-corruption and financial controls under the incumbent administration.","contrary_evidence":["The report also says officials would pursue the FATF recommendations and high-level commitment."],"lenses":["5B.5","5B.7","5B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Top Congo presidential adviser resigns after allegedly requesting bribe on tape","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-09-16","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/top-congo-presidential-adviser-resigns-after-allegedly-requested-bribe-on-tape-2894087","claim":"Reuters reported that a top adviser to President Felix Tshisekedi resigned after being caught on tape allegedly negotiating a corrupt mineral deal.","locator":"lines 418-421","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting on a concrete corruption scandal involving a presidential adviser.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target-period corruption evidence.","ruler_attribution":"High: the adviser was a close figure in Tshisekedi's current cabinet and election network.","contrary_evidence":["The adviser denied wrongdoing and the presidency said violators would suffer consequences."],"lenses":["5B.2","5B.5","5B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"I Will Take My Percentage: Congolese Presidential Adviser Caught on Tape Negotiating Corrupt Mineral Deal","publisher":"OCCRP","publication_date":"2022-09-15","url":"https://www.occrp.org/en/investigation/i-will-take-my-percentage-congolese-presidential-adviser-caught-on-tape-negotiating-corrupt-mineral-deal","claim":"OCCRP said the adviser described his closeness to President Felix Tshisekedi and was recorded offering access to mining licenses in exchange for a stake in a joint venture.","locator":"lines 32-33 and 117-119","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary investigative reporting with direct recording-based allegations.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target-period corruption evidence.","ruler_attribution":"High: the conduct was tied to a close presidential adviser invoking access to Tshisekedi.","contrary_evidence":["The recording appears to be an apparent sting operation, so the evidentiary chain should be kept explicit."],"lenses":["5B.2","5B.5","5B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"DR Congo: Martial Law Brings Crackdown in East","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2022-03-22","url":"https://www.hrw.org/news/2022/03/22/dr-congo-martial-law-brings-crackdown-east","claim":"Human Rights Watch said the military and police curtailed freedom of expression, used lethal force against peaceful demonstrations, and arbitrarily detained and prosecuted activists, journalists, and political opposition members under martial law.","locator":"lines 616-616","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Detailed human-rights reporting on a clearly identified state policy in 2022.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target-period rights and governance evidence.","ruler_attribution":"High: the crackdown followed a government-imposed state of siege under Tshisekedi's administration.","contrary_evidence":["The government framed martial law as a response to insecurity, but the report argues rights were still suppressed."],"lenses":["5B.4","5B.6","5B.7","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Child Labor and Human Rights Violations in the Mining Industry of the Democratic Republic of Congo","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2022-07-14","url":"https://www.hrw.org/news/2022/07/14/child-labor-and-human-rights-violations-mining-industry-democratic-republic-congo","claim":"HRW said Tshisekedi's administration had made many promises of reform but little action, and that corrupt and abusive practices and repression against journalists, activists, critics, and peaceful protesters had continued or escalated.","locator":"lines 633-635","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct testimony from a major rights NGO grounded in contemporaneous reporting.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target-period governance and welfare evidence.","ruler_attribution":"High: the statement explicitly assesses Tshisekedi's administration.","contrary_evidence":["The same testimony notes some positive early steps such as releasing political prisoners."],"lenses":["5B.2","5B.5","5B.7","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Child Labor and Human Rights Violations in the Mining Industry of the Democratic Republic of Congo","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2022-07-14","url":"https://www.hrw.org/news/2022/07/14/child-labor-and-human-rights-violations-mining-industry-democratic-republic-congo","claim":"HRW said an activist died after denouncing embezzlement of mining royalties and that police violently dispersed an opposition sit-in over the election law, injuring and arresting protesters.","locator":"lines 636-636","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous human-rights testimony with specific incident detail.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target-period evidence on corruption and coercive response.","ruler_attribution":"High: the incidents are attributed to state actors under the incumbent administration.","contrary_evidence":["The report also shows the government remained under domestic and international pressure to reform."],"lenses":["5B.5","5B.7","5B.8","5B.10"]}

Search ledger: candidates found about 40, documents opened 18, duplicate families removed 12, irrelevant or out-of-period items 6, inaccessible items 4, accepted distinct URLs 15.

Material gaps and next best directions:
- Strongest gap is direct 2022 evidence on appointment quality and whether Tshisekedi empowered competent economic professionals versus loyalists. I have ministry names and IMF meeting records, but not a clean attribution source on appointment merit or delegation.
- I still lack direct 2022 evidence on actual household distribution effects from the budget and reforms, especially by region and income group, beyond broad poverty and shared-growth findings.
- I do not yet have a clean 2022 execution source for whether the budgeted anti-corruption, VAT, treasury, and social-transfer plans were delivered at scale by year-end.
- Next best sources would be the 2022 EITI country report, a 2022 Cour des comptes or IGF audit on mining royalties and budget execution, INS household survey material, and any 2022/2023 World Bank or IMF documents focused on PFM execution, tax administration, and social spending outcomes.
